---
description: Repository-first workflow and implementation quality
alwaysApply: true
---
- Inspect actual files and project conventions before editing; don't assume paths/features from plans exist.
- Preserve Next.js, TypeScript, MySQL, Railway, and `n8n/` unless verified reasons justify change.
- State a short plan and risks before multi-file changes.
- Make the smallest coherent change; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Verify package scripts from `package.json`; never fabricate test results.
- Report changed files, commands and outcomes, migration/deploy steps, and unresolved risks.
- Ask before production, destructive, or consequential changes.
